QEMU's emulated Intel flash (hw/block/pflash_cfi01.c, the 0xe8 block write
cycle: master line 608, v10.0.0 line 602) opens its write buffer only when the
word count is non-zero:

    if (pfl->blk_offset == -1 && pfl->counter) {
        pflash_blk_write_start(pfl, offset);
    }
    if (!pfl->ro && (pfl->blk_offset != -1)) {
        pflash_data_write(pfl, offset, value, width, be);
    } else {
        pfl->status |= 0x10; /* Programming error */
    }

On Intel CFI a count of N writes N+1 words. A buffer write of exactly one bank
word (count 0) therefore never opens the buffer. It fails with SR.4, and the
status poll after the confirm times out. On the qemu-virt flash (two x16 chips
in a 32-bit bank), UBI's nor_erase_prepare writes one 4-byte word to clear a
PEB header before each erase. So the first erase fails ("buffer write error
(status timeout)", "cannot invalidate PEB"), and UBI and UBIFS turn read-only.

The qemu-armhf board exists only to run under QEMU, so the workaround lives in
its kernel: a chunk that fits inside one bank word takes the word program
(0x40) instead of the buffer write. The flash holds the same bytes either way.
A chunk spanning two kvecs keeps the buffer write; the single-buffer path UBI
uses never produces one.

This patch is carried only by the qemu-armhf board kernel.

Base: stable linux v6.12.111 e2acc2211022246c77740d5df08265cc27eedcc5

--- a/drivers/mtd/chips/cfi_cmdset_0001.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/chips/cfi_cmdset_0001.c
@@ -1913,8 +1913,23 @@
 
 		if (size > len)
 			size = len;
-		ret = do_write_buffer(map, &cfi->chips[chipnum],
-				      ofs, &vecs, &vec_seek, size);
+		/* QEMU's pflash_cfi01 fails a buffer write of one bank word
+		   (word count 0), so such a chunk takes the word program. */
+		if ((ofs & (map_bankwidth(map)-1)) + size <= map_bankwidth(map) &&
+		    vecs->iov_len - vec_seek >= size) {
+			size_t written = 0;
+
+			ret = cfi_intelext_write_words(mtd, (chipnum << cfi->chipshift) + ofs,
+						       size, &written,
+						       vecs->iov_base + vec_seek);
+			vec_seek += size;
+			if (vec_seek == vecs->iov_len) {
+				vecs++;
+				vec_seek = 0;
+			}
+		} else
+			ret = do_write_buffer(map, &cfi->chips[chipnum],
+					      ofs, &vecs, &vec_seek, size);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
